  "cli_result_text": "Submitted. Summary of the mapping this file set supports:\n\n**Babel side** (`packages/babel-plugin-proposal-decorators/src/index.ts`) dispatches on `options.legacy`/`options.version`: `legacy: true` (or `version: \"legacy\"`) routes to `transformer-legacy.ts` (the stage-2 TS-compatible `__decorate`-style transform, forked from `babel-plugin-proposal-decorators-legacy`); any stage-3 version (`2021-12`+, the default) routes into `@babel/helper-create-class-features-plugin`'s `decorators.ts`, which implements the TC39 stage-3 semantics and **emits no `Reflect.metadata`/design-type calls at all** \u2014 that machinery only exists in the legacy path. `babel-plugin-syntax-decorators/src/index.ts` is where `legacy`/`version` get validated and turned into parser plugin flags. `babel-preset-typescript/src/index.ts` shows decorators aren't part of the TS preset itself \u2014 the customer must have `plugin-proposal-decorators` ordered *before* `plugin-transform-typescript` in their plugin list (preset-typescript doesn't include it), since type annotations must still be visible when `legacy` mode reads parameter/property type info.\n\n**SWC side**: `crates/swc_ecma_transforms_typescript/src/typescript.rs` (+ `lib.rs`) proves the TS strip transform (`StripImportExport` \u2192 `StripType` \u2192 `transform`) does **not touch decorators at all** \u2014 it's purely type erasure. Decorators are a fully separate pass, `swc_ecma_transforms_proposal::decorators::decorators()` (`decorators/mod.rs`), wired in from `crates/swc/src/config/mod.rs` where `jsc.transform.legacyDecorator` / `decoratorMetadata` live. Critically, `decorators/mod.rs` shows: if `legacy == false` and `emit_metadata == true`, it hits `unimplemented!(\"emitting decorator metadata while using new proposal\")` \u2014 metadata emission is *only* wired through `decorators/legacy/mod.rs`, which calls into `decorators/legacy/metadata.rs` (a direct port of `babel-plugin-transform-typescript-metadata`, emitting `design:type`/`design:paramtypes`/`design:returntype` via the `ts_metadata`/`ts_decorate` helpers \u2014 SWC's `Reflect.metadata` equivalent).\n\n**The divergence**: Nest.js DI metadata requires the *legacy* decorator lowering plus metadata emission on both sides. In Babel that's `legacy: true` on `plugin-proposal-decorators`. In SWC it's `jsc.transform.legacyDecorator: true` **and** `jsc.transform.decoratorMetadata: true` together \u2014 if the customer's swc config left `legacyDecorator` unset/false (SWC's default targets the modern stage-3-ish proposal) while only setting `decoratorMetadata: true`, or set neither, the decorators pass either silently uses the non-metadata code path or never emits the `Reflect.metadata` calls Nest's `IoC`/`getMetadata` container depends on \u2014 explaining \"classes construct, DI table never populates.\"",
